    {
      "id": "US-1116",
      "title": "Phase M: exclude completed stories from semantic dedup comparison set",
      "description": "Phase M currently compares every new story candidate against ALL stories in prd.json, including the 309+ completed ones (passes: true). This means a new story about 'improving X' gets rejected as a near-duplicate of the completed story 'implement X', even though they are genuinely different work. The dedup filter should only compare new candidates against PENDING stories (passes: false). Completed stories are done — a candidate that resembles a completed story is an extension or improvement, not a true duplicate. Fix lib/merge_stories.py (or the relevant dedup function): when building the comparison corpus, filter to only stories where passes is False.",
      "priority": "critical",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "Phase M dedup only compares new candidates against stories where passes == False",
        "A new candidate with >85% title similarity to a completed (passes: true) story is NOT rejected as a duplicate",
        "A new candidate with >85% title similarity to a pending (passes: false) story IS still rejected",
        "uv run pytest tests/test_merge_stories.py covers the completed-story exclusion case",
        "When prd.json has 300+ completed stories and 0 pending, Phase M merges new candidates normally"
      ],
      "passes": false,
      "dependencies": [],
      "filesTouch": [
        "lib/merge_stories.py",
        "tests/test_merge_stories.py"
      ],
      "estimatedComplexity": "small",
      "tags": [
        "phase-m",
        "dedup",
        "bugfix"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "US-1117",
      "title": "Auto-archive completed stories when prd.json exceeds SPIRAL_AUTO_ARCHIVE_THRESHOLD",
      "description": "When prd.json accumulates hundreds of completed stories (passes: true), the file becomes slow to parse, dedup becomes ineffective, and git diffs become noisy. Add a config var SPIRAL_AUTO_ARCHIVE_THRESHOLD (default: 100). At the start of each iteration, if the count of completed stories exceeds this threshold, automatically run the archive-done logic (equivalent to `spiral.sh --archive-done`) before Phase A begins. The archive must be committed to git immediately (auto-commit with message 'chore: auto-archive N completed stories') so the auto-stash mechanism does not revert it.",
      "priority": "high",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "spiral.config.sh has SPIRAL_AUTO_ARCHIVE_THRESHOLD variable (default 100)",
        "At the start of each iteration, if completed story count >= threshold, archive-done runs automatically",
        "The resulting prd.json and prd-archive.json are committed to git before Phase A runs",
        "Log message: [auto-archive] Archived N completed stories (threshold: M)",
        "Setting SPIRAL_AUTO_ARCHIVE_THRESHOLD=0 disables auto-archive",
        "uv run pytest tests/test_auto_archive.py covers threshold trigger and git commit"
      ],
      "passes": false,
      "dependencies": [],
      "filesTouch": [
        "spiral.sh",
        "spiral.config.sh",
        "lib/commands/archive.py",
        "tests/test_auto_archive.py"
      ],
      "estimatedComplexity": "medium",
      "tags": [
        "phase-a",
        "archive",
        "maintenance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "US-1118",
      "title": "Phase A: inject completed story titles into AI suggest prompt to avoid near-duplicates",
      "description": "The Phase A LLM prompt does not include the list of already-completed stories, so the AI generates suggestions that are near-duplicates of completed work. Inject a summary of completed story titles (grouped by theme/epic) into the Phase A system prompt with the instruction: 'The following stories are ALREADY DONE — do not suggest them again or close variations.' This makes the LLM generate genuinely novel stories rather than retracing completed ground. To keep the prompt compact, send only titles (not full descriptions), grouped by epicId, truncated to SPIRAL_AI_SUGGEST_HISTORY_LIMIT entries (default 50 most recent).",
      "priority": "high",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "Phase A prompt includes a completed-stories section listing done story titles",
        "Completed stories injected are grouped by epicId and limited to SPIRAL_AI_SUGGEST_HISTORY_LIMIT (default 50)",
        "spiral.config.sh has SPIRAL_AI_SUGGEST_HISTORY_LIMIT variable (default 50, 0 = disable injection)",
        "Phase A output has measurably lower overlap with completed story titles (test: TF-IDF similarity < 0.7 avg)",
        "Token cost increase for the Phase A call is < 500 tokens per iteration at the default limit"
      ],
      "passes": false,
      "dependencies": [],
      "filesTouch": [
        "spiral.sh",
        "spiral.config.sh",
        "lib/phases/phase_a_suggest.sh"
      ],
      "estimatedComplexity": "small",
      "tags": [
        "phase-a",
