      "id": "US-1119",
      "title": "Phase M: emit a warning and lower dedup threshold when 100% of candidates are rejected",
      "description": "When Phase M rejects ALL candidates in an iteration (0 new stories added), it silently moves on. This makes it impossible to detect the 'dense backlog deadlock' without reading logs carefully. Add detection: if merge complete with 0 new stories AND input candidates > 0, emit a structured warning: [merge] WARNING: All N candidates rejected as duplicates. Consider --archive-done or lowering SPIRAL_SEMANTIC_DEDUP_THRESHOLD. Additionally, if this happens for SPIRAL_DEDUP_FALLBACK_ITERS consecutive iterations (default 3), automatically lower the effective threshold by 0.05 for that iteration only (floor: 0.60) as a one-time fallback. Log the temporary threshold: [merge] Applying fallback threshold 0.80 (normal: 0.85).",
